      "id": "claim_b586aca9bdf046058ff709d5282dfa37",
      "statement": "AGENTS.md requires an ADR before implementation when a change introduces or alters a product capability/user-visible behavior, cross-package protocol/schema, architectural boundary/ownership, auth/privacy/storage/trust, browser routing/targeting/lifecycle, or a materially architecture-changing dependency; an ADR is usually unnecessary for bug fixes, tests, doc corrections, behavior-preserving refactors, narrow tooling, or already-covered implementation.",
      "evidence": [
